WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.337
Hi, I'm Bagel!

00:00:02.337 --> 00:00:06.177
This K2-Horizon model puts a mixture of experts inside attention itself.

00:00:06.177 --> 00:00:09.318
Here's how it does that without growing the cache.

00:00:10.517 --> 00:00:15.086
Route the value projection through sixty-four experts, but mix them before the cache.

00:00:15.086 --> 00:00:18.250
Then the cache stores one ordinary value per token.

00:00:19.483 --> 00:00:24.304
Where attention had one value projection, this has sixty-four, and each token runs four.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:27.998
Each expert is a whole value projection, to eight heads of

00:00:27.998 --> 00:00:29.188
a hundred and twenty-eight.

00:00:29.608 --> 00:00:33.270
Each output goes through a non-linear activation, so the value is no

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:35.406
longer a linear map of the token.

00:00:35.826 --> 00:00:39.358
And the router's sigmoid scores, renormalised and scaled by two and a

00:00:39.358 --> 00:00:40.535
half, weight the four.

00:00:41.967 --> 00:00:46.002
A router reads each token and picks four of the sixty-four value experts.

00:00:46.422 --> 00:00:50.341
Their outputs are summed and reshaped to eight heads of a hundred

00:00:50.341 --> 00:00:53.280
and twenty-eight: exactly what a plain grouped-query layer writes.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.131
Only then is the cache updated.

00:00:56.131 --> 00:01:01.397
It holds ordinary shapes, so FlashAttention runs unmodified, and never learns routing happened.

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:06.518
So the cost moves from cache to weights: sixty-four times the parameters,

00:01:06.518 --> 00:01:09.164
four times the decode work, the same cache.

00:01:10.217 --> 00:01:13.146
But no extra cache isn't a small cache.

00:01:13.146 --> 00:01:17.539
All forty-eight layers are full attention, so one sequence at the full

00:01:17.539 --> 00:01:19.004
context holds ninety-six gigabytes.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.728
Collapse the mixture before the cache, and everything downstream stays ordinary.

00:01:23.728 --> 00:01:26.697
The cost moves from the cache to the weights.

00:01:27.983 --> 00:01:32.107
To recap: sixty-four value experts, mixed before the cache, paid for in

00:01:32.107 --> 00:01:33.482
weights instead of memory.

00:01:33.902 --> 00:01:35.995
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:36.593
I'm Bagel.

00:01:36.593 --> 00:01:36.892
Bye!
